<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Sasani rights offer raises 51 million rand.</title>
<headline>Sasani rights offer raises 51 million rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Sasani Ltd said on Thursday that a rights offer to its shareholders had been 99.5 percent subscribed and raised 51 million rand before expenses.</p>
<p>Sasani, quoted in the media sector, reverse-listed into the Crendell cash shell on Monday. It acquired The Video Lab Group which forms its core business.</p>
<p>Sasani shareholders were offerred the stock at a price of 18 cents a share.</p>
<p>The company is a joint venture between Interleisure Ltd, Video lab Group and a black empowerment group, Msomi Ventures.</p>
<p>Sasani has said in the past that it is looking to expand in the media sector locally and internationally.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
